---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const site = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://usdtoworld.com');
const breadcrumbSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: site.toString() },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: new URL('/privacy-policy', site).toString() },
  ],
};
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | UsdtoWorld"
  description="Read UsdtoWorld's privacy policy covering what data we collect, how local storage is used, and your choices."
  path="/privacy-policy"
  schema={[breadcrumbSchema]}
>
  <div class="container page-hero">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/privacy-policy' }]} />
  </div>
  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated-note">Last updated: October 3, 2026</p>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how UsdtoWorld ("we", "us", "our") — operated from Office No. 202, P4,
        Ground, Shagun Tower, AB Rd, Near Vijay Nagar Square, Scheme 54 PU4, Indore, Madhya Pradesh 452010,
        India — handles information when you use usdtoworld.com. It is written to be read, not skimmed past, so
        each section says what happens, why, and what you can do about it.
      </p>

      <div class="plain-summary">
        <strong>In plain terms:</strong> you don't need an account to use UsdtoWorld. We don't sell your
        data. We use Google Analytics and Google AdSense, which set their own cookies, and your theme,
        language, and recent conversions are stored only in your own browser. If you email us, we keep that
        message to reply to you.
      </div>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        UsdtoWorld is designed to work without an account, and the converter never asks for personal
        information. The limited data that may be processed falls into four groups:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Local device storage:</strong> your theme preference, language choice, recent conversions, and recently viewed pages are saved in your browser's local storage and are not sent to our servers. The site also uses a service worker, a small browser feature that keeps copies of pages and the last rate you loaded so the site still works offline.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage analytics:</strong> we use Google Analytics to understand aggregate traffic, such as which pages are visited, roughly where visitors are, and how long they stay. Google Analytics uses cookies and may process your IP address; see Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a> for details.</li>
        <li><strong>Server and security logs:</strong> our hosting and security provider, Cloudflare, processes standard technical data such as IP address, browser type and request time in order to deliver the site, block abuse, and keep it available.</li>
        <li><strong>Contact form submissions:</strong> if you message us, we keep your name, email address and message so we can reply and, where relevant, fix the problem you reported.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <p>
        We use information only to operate and improve the site, understand which guides and converters are
        useful, keep the service secure, show advertising that helps fund it, and respond to messages. We do not
        sell personal information, and we do not use the contents of your conversions to build a profile of you,
        because those stay in your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Live exchange rate data ultimately comes from ExchangeRate-API (open.er-api.com), a third-party rate
        provider. That request is made server-side by our own infrastructure, not directly from your browser, so
        your browser only communicates with usdtoworld.com when it fetches a rate. Fonts are served from our own
        domain. The only third parties that your browser may contact directly are Google, for analytics and
        advertising, as described below.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google AdSense to display advertising on content pages of this site. Third-party vendors, including
        Google, use cookies and similar technologies to serve ads based on your previous visits to this and other
        websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your
        visit to our site and other sites on the internet. You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
        Google's <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ads Settings</a>,
        or opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalised advertising at
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.aboutads.info</a>. You can
        read how Google uses information from sites that use its services at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
        Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are covered by Google's
        additional consent requirements for personalised ads. We do not show ads on error, maintenance or other
        status pages that carry no content of their own.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can clear or block cookies and local storage at any time in your browser settings. Doing so may reset
        your theme, language and recent conversions, but the converter will keep working.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights and choices</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, laws such as India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and the EU and UK
        GDPR give you rights over personal data, including the right to ask what we hold about you, to correct it, and
        to ask us to delete it. Because we hold very little, the main data we can act on is anything you sent through the
        <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>. Send a request there or to usdtoworld@gmail.com and we will respond within a
        reasonable time. You may also object to personalised advertising using the Google tools above.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and security</h2>
      <p>
        We keep contact messages only as long as needed to resolve your question and for a reasonable period afterwards.
        Analytics data is retained according to Google Analytics' own settings. The site is served over HTTPS and we limit
        the data we collect so there is less to protect, but no internet service can promise absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>UsdtoWorld is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from them. If you believe a child has sent us information, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy as the site or the law changes. Material changes will be reflected by updating the date above, so it is worth checking it from time to time.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy can be sent via our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a> or to usdtoworld@gmail.com.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
